To run the same code inline on multiple named variables in C++, you can use a lambda function or a function pointer with a template. Here's a concise way to do it:

```cpp
#include <iostream>

template<typename Func>
void runOnMultipleVariables(Func func, int a, int b, int c) {
    func(a);
    func(b);
    func(c);
}

